# The parsed pattern, which every tier reads: the reference interpreter walks it, the analysis decides a tier from
# it, the compiler turns it into a program, and the native tier writes it back as an engine's syntax. One tree, so a
# pattern means what ./syntax.tree read it as and nothing else (note/term/stdlib/regex-engine.md).
#
# A set of code points is a list of numbers, a start and an end (both included) per range, sorted, never overlapping
# or touching: [48, 57, 97, 122] is 0-9 and a-z. The `i` flag is applied when the pattern is read, so a letter under
# `i` is already the set of its case class and nothing later folds case, except a back reference, which compares
# text it cannot know in advance.

mark stable

load @term/base/exception
  find mismatch
  find excess

# one node of a pattern
form piece
  # matches the empty text
  case blank
  # one code point, exactly
  case letter
    link point, like number
  # one code point in the set
  case ranges
    link set
      like list
        like number
  # a zero-width test of the position: one of the edge kinds below
  case edge
    link kind, like number
  # each part in turn
  case chain
    link parts
      like list
        like piece
  # the first part that leads to a match, in order
  case choice
    link parts
      like list
        like piece
  # the body repeated from `least` to `most` times (`most` -1 is unbounded). Greedy takes as many as it can first,
  # lazy as few, and possessive takes as many as it can and never gives one back
  case loop
    link body, like piece
    link least, like number
    link most, like number
    link greedy, like boolean
    link possessive, like boolean
  # a capturing group: `index` counts from 1 in the order the groups open, and `label` is the name, empty for an unnamed one
  case group
    link body, like piece
    link index, like number
    link label, like text
  # an atomic group: the body's first match, never revisited
  case atom
    link body, like piece
  # a lookaround: whether the body matches ahead of the position (or behind it), consuming nothing
  case look
    link body, like piece
    link behind, like boolean
    link negate, like boolean
  # the text group `index` last captured, compared code point by code point, by case class when `fold` is set. A
  # group that took no part matches the empty text
  case refer
    link index, like number
    link fold, like boolean

# the edge kinds
host edge-text-start, code 0
host edge-text-end, code 1
host edge-line-start, code 2
host edge-line-end, code 3
host edge-word, code 4
host edge-not-word, code 5

# a pattern that cannot be read: where (in code points) and why
form pattern-mismatch
  like mismatch
    bind note, <Not a pattern>
    link at, like number
    link reason, like text

# a match that did more work than its budget allows. Only the backtracking tier can raise it, and only for a pattern
# whose meaning has no known linear-time algorithm (a back reference, an atomic group the analysis could not rewrite)
form pattern-budget
  like excess
    bind note, <Pattern work over its limit>
    link at, like number

# whether the piece is a test of the position alone, which a quantifier may not repeat
task is-zero-width
  take p, like piece
  like boolean
  fork case, read p
    case blank
      send back, true
    case edge
      send back, true
    case look
      send back, true
    case letter
      send back, false
    case ranges
      send back, false
    case chain
      send back, false
    case choice
      send back, false
    case loop
      send back, false
    case group
      send back, false
    case atom
      send back, false
    case refer
      send back, false

task refuse-pattern
  take at, like number
  take reason, like text
  like piece
  halt pattern-mismatch
    bind thing, text <pattern>
    bind at, read at
    bind reason, read reason
